# Spec Delta — F-0NN Feature name

**Baseline:** `.product/project-spec/` @ `0000000`

<!--
The baseline is named, never copied. Quote at most one line for context inside a
CHANGED block. Re-base against the current ref if project-spec/ has moved since.

Sections appear in merge order and are applied in that order:
  RENAMED -> REMOVED -> CHANGED -> ADDED
Omit any section with no operations. Do not invent verbs.
-->

## Out of Scope

- Adjacent thing a reader would expect this feature to change, and the reason it does not.

<!--
Bounded on purpose. Do NOT add an "Unchanged" section: that set is the complement of
this delta over the whole baseline, so it can never be complete, and its incompleteness
is indistinguishable from an oversight.
-->

## RENAMED

### XX-01 Old name -> XX-01 New name

**Scenarios:** references that carry across the rename, by id and path — or `none`, verified with a search.

What else moves with the name, if anything.

<!--
RENAMED is its own verb because a rename expressed as REMOVED plus ADDED loses every
reference to the old identifier, and both halves look individually valid. Renaming the
identifier as well as the name breaks every reference: do it only when you mean to.
-->

## REMOVED

### XX-02 Section that ceases to exist

**Scenarios:** every acceptance criterion, requirement id, test file and user flow that referenced this, each with its new home or an explicit reason it is obsolete.

Why it is gone.

## CHANGED

### XX-03 Section that survives with different meaning

**Scenarios:** references affected, and their status after the change.

**Was:** one line, quoted for context only.
**Now:** the new statement.

## ADDED

### XX-04 New section

The new content, in the shape project-spec/ expects.

